IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc19-s492-31`

-- ccc19-tests-s492-31.l4 -- tests for ccc19-s492-31.l4 (Criminal Code (Canada) s 492.31, Alternative Remedies to Stay of Proceedings).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the subsection named beside it, before the run. A failing assertion is a finding.

§ `s 492.31(1) -- A court shall not order a stay of proceedings as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay unless it is satisfied that no other remedy would be appropriate and just`

-- a stay as a result of the finding, the court is not satisfied that no other remedy would be appropriate and just: barred
#ASSERT `s 492.31(1) the court is barred from ordering a stay of proceedings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a stay as a result of the finding, the court is satisfied: the "unless" is met, so this subsection does not bar it
#ASSERT `s 492.31(1) the court is barred from ordering a stay of proceedings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a stay that is not as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay: the subsection does not speak to it
#ASSERT `s 492.31(1) the court is barred from ordering a stay of proceedings` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 492.31(1) the court is barred from ordering a stay of proceedings` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The regulative rule. Expected, from the text: ordering the stay when the court is not satisfied is a BREACH by the court; ordering it when satisfied is not a breach (the guard rejects the match);
-- with no event the prohibition stands.
#TRACE `s 492.31(1) the court shall not order a stay of proceedings` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 492.31(1) order a stay of proceedings as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay` FALSE AT 3

#TRACE `s 492.31(1) the court shall not order a stay of proceedings` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 492.31(1) order a stay of proceedings as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay` TRUE AT 3

#TRACE `s 492.31(1) the court shall not order a stay of proceedings` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 50)

§ `s 492.31(2) -- In determining whether a remedy other than a stay of proceedings is appropriate and just, the court shall take into account the following factors`

-- Each of the five named factors, (a) to (e), in that determination: the court must take it into account
#ASSERT `s 492.31(2) the court must take the factor into account` TRUE `s 492.31(2)(a) the stage of the proceedings during which the finding of unreasonable delay is made or during which the delay became unreasonable` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.31(2) the court must take the factor into account` TRUE `s 492.31(2)(b) the impact that a stay of proceedings is likely to have on any victim of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.31(2) the court must take the factor into account` TRUE `s 492.31(2)(c) the prejudice that has been or would be suffered by the accused or offender as a result of unreasonable delay` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.31(2) the court must take the factor into account` TRUE `s 492.31(2)(d) the public’s confidence in the administration of justice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.31(2) the court must take the factor into account` TRUE `s 492.31(2)(e) the interest that society has in having a final decision on the merits` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a factor that is none of (a) to (e): the list is not closed with "only", so not covered
#ASSERT `s 492.31(2) the court must take the factor into account` TRUE `s 492.31(2) another factor, not named in paragraphs (a) to (e)` EQUALS NOTHING
-- not in that determination: the "In determining" is not met, whatever the factor
#ASSERT `s 492.31(2) the court must take the factor into account` FALSE `s 492.31(2)(c) the prejudice that has been or would be suffered by the accused or offender as a result of unreasonable delay` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 492.31(2) the court must take the factor into account` FALSE `s 492.31(2) another factor, not named in paragraphs (a) to (e)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The regulative rule, for factor (c): the standing obligation; performed for (c): FULFILLED; performed only for (a): the guard rejects it and the duty for (c) stands; not determining: nothing owed.
#TRACE `s 492.31(2) the duty of the court to take the factor into account` TRUE `s 492.31(2)(c) the prejudice that has been or would be suffered by the accused or offender as a result of unreasonable delay` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

#TRACE `s 492.31(2) the duty of the court to take the factor into account` TRUE `s 492.31(2)(c) the prejudice that has been or would be suffered by the accused or offender as a result of unreasonable delay` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 492.31(2) take the factor into account in determining whether a remedy other than a stay of proceedings is appropriate and just` `s 492.31(2)(c) the prejudice that has been or would be suffered by the accused or offender as a result of unreasonable delay` AT 2

#TRACE `s 492.31(2) the duty of the court to take the factor into account` TRUE `s 492.31(2)(c) the prejudice that has been or would be suffered by the accused or offender as a result of unreasonable delay` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 492.31(2) take the factor into account in determining whether a remedy other than a stay of proceedings is appropriate and just` `s 492.31(2)(a) the stage of the proceedings during which the finding of unreasonable delay is made or during which the delay became unreasonable` AT 2

#TRACE `s 492.31(2) the duty of the court to take the factor into account` FALSE `s 492.31(2)(c) the prejudice that has been or would be suffered by the accused or offender as a result of unreasonable delay` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)
